al_tokens_map.json:   0%|          | 0.00/99.0 [00:00<?, ?B/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["['▁I', '▁love', '▁Machine', '▁Learning', '.']\n"]}],"source":["from transformers import AutoTokenizer\n","\n","tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\n","    \"google/mt5-small\"\n",")\n","\n","tokens = tokenizer.tokenize(text)\n","print(tokens)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"dde9d112","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005002,"end_time":"2026-11-05T16:44:16.855233+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-05T16:44:16.850231+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["The tokenizer evaluates possible segmentations using probabilities learned from its training data.\n","\n","It selects a segmentation with a high probability according to its model.\n","\n","The vocabulary is gradually reduced by removing tokens that contribute least to the overall likelihood.\n","\n","Where is it used?\n","\n","SentencePiece supports Unigram and BPE tokenization. Some models, including T5 and several multilingual models, use Unigram-based tokenization.\n","\n","### Comparison of tokenization algorithms\n","\n","| Algorithm | Main mechanism                              | Example association     |\n","| --------- | ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n","| BPE       | Repeatedly merges frequent pairs            | GPT-family tokenizers   |\n","| WordPiece | Selects merges using likelihood improvement | BERT                    |\n","| Unigram   | Starts large and removes less useful pieces | T5/SentencePiece models |\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"90b92977","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005049,"end_time":"2026-11-05T16:44:16.865277+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-05T16:44:16.860228+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Vocabulary\n","\n","A vocabulary is a collection of all tokens that a tokenizer knows.\n","\n","Imagine a small vocab